# Composition-Only Component API

RefineUI component APIs are **composable only**.

## Rules
- **MUST**: Components must be usable via slot/subcomponent composition.
- **MUST NOT**: Do not add convenience prop APIs like `title`, `description`, `items`, `actions`, `onClose`.
- **MUST NOT**: Do not add single-prop render paths that bypass existing composition.
- **MUST**: Root components are containers only; actual UI is split into subcomponents.
- **MUST**: State/presentation/behavior extensions are exposed via subcomponents (e.g. `ComponentHeader`, `ComponentBody`, `ComponentAction`).
- **MUST**: Documentation examples show the composable API only.

## Migration
- Remove legacy convenience APIs incrementally.
- When removing, update `packages/react/src/index.ts`, each component `index.ts`, and docs previews/mdx together.
- Validate with `@refineui/react` and `@refineui/documentation` builds after changes.